 It's such a boomer opinion to have.

00:26:01.480 --> 00:26:04.320
 I'm not saying you're a boomer, I'm just saying.

00:26:04.320 --> 00:26:07.160
 Oh, yeah, that's got daily express article written all over it,

00:26:07.160 --> 00:26:10.320
 like, what's wrong with a bit of good old British fog, you know?

00:26:10.320 --> 00:26:11.600
 And it's the immigrants fault.

00:26:11.600 --> 00:26:12.920
 Yeah, it's great.

00:26:12.920 --> 00:26:15.800
 And you know what, the young people couldn't handle it anyway.

00:26:15.800 --> 00:26:17.120
 I don't think it would be in the express

00:26:17.120 --> 00:26:19.200
 because it's probably due to climate change.

00:26:19.200 --> 00:26:20.280
 Oh, OK.

00:26:20.280 --> 00:26:22.480
 So, yeah, this is quite a few studies

00:26:22.480 --> 00:26:23.840
 have been done over the last few years,

00:26:23.840 --> 00:26:27.440
 and every single one shows a big decrease in fog.

00:26:27.440 --> 00:26:30.640
 2009 studies showed that in Europe, there is a 50% drop

00:26:30.640 --> 00:26:34.000
 in low visibility events, which just is fog mist,

00:26:34.000 --> 00:26:36.680
 haze, all of that stuff, since the 1970s.

00:26:36.680 --> 00:26:41.680
 And in 2010, the back of the university looked at America,

00:26:41.680 --> 00:26:46.320
 and they found that fog has declined 33% since 1951.

00:26:46.320 --> 00:26:48.720
 What it seems is that basically climate change

00:26:48.720 --> 00:26:51.520
 means that as the oceans warm, the conditions

00:26:51.520 --> 00:26:55.600
 you need for sea fog, especially, you need like a cold water

00:26:55.600 --> 00:26:57.600
 surface in order to the fog to form,

00:26:57.600 --> 00:27:00.880
 because it's when the warmer from the water kind of hits the land,

00:27:00.880 --> 00:27:02.880
 you just don't really get those conditions anymore.

00:27:02.880 --> 00:27:05.600
 So we just get less fog than we used to, and it's important.

00:27:05.600 --> 00:27:09.120
 Fog is the new moss.

00:27:09.120 --> 00:27:11.560
 I mean, fog is really important.

00:27:11.560 --> 00:27:14.520
 So there's lots of crops which use fog in places

00:27:14.520 --> 00:27:16.640
 where it doesn't rain so much.

00:27:16.640 --> 00:27:20.640
 For instance, in California, where they make lots of letters,

00:27:20.640 --> 00:27:24.160
 or they make lots of strawberries, is the fog which nourishes them

00:27:24.160 --> 00:27:26.000
 and keeps them hydrated.

00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:29.360
 And in cities, the fog can sort of move away pollutants

00:27:29.360 --> 00:27:31.840
 from the air, so it's really useful there as well.

00:27:31.840 --> 00:27:34.160
 We need our fog, and it's all going.

00:27:34.160 --> 00:27:35.200
 Why isn't that the fog?

