 Keen, very keen.

00:28:14.080 --> 00:28:17.600
 But there was a company in America that did codes, still do codes.

00:28:17.600 --> 00:28:19.200
 I think they were called London Town initially.

00:28:19.200 --> 00:28:20.800
 They changed their name to London Fog.

00:28:20.800 --> 00:28:22.720
 But I think that's because it was famous back in the day.

00:28:22.720 --> 00:28:24.640
 But the '70s, it was gone.

00:28:24.640 --> 00:28:26.160
 Poor. We nailed it.

00:28:26.160 --> 00:28:27.920
 This was the big smog, wasn't it?

00:28:27.920 --> 00:28:30.560
 That was, yeah, Victorian era, start of the 20th century.

00:28:30.560 --> 00:28:31.760
 Bit of a disaster in London.

00:28:31.760 --> 00:28:32.880
 No one could see anything.

00:28:32.880 --> 00:28:35.600
 Americans flocked, because Tomas Cook organized

00:28:35.600 --> 00:28:36.720
 four holidays, apparently.

00:28:36.720 --> 00:28:39.440
 But it was, so I think that was quite bad.

00:28:39.440 --> 00:28:42.000
 And then we had the Clean Air Act in 1956,

00:28:42.000 --> 00:28:44.240
 which is kind of an amazing success story,

00:28:44.240 --> 00:28:46.400
 which basically sorted it out.

00:28:46.400 --> 00:28:48.720
 But it was a massive issue before that.

00:28:48.720 --> 00:28:51.520
 And it was particularly an issue for Hollywood, in fact,

00:28:51.520 --> 00:28:52.880
 and for filmmakers.

00:28:52.880 --> 00:28:55.360
 So it wasn't just bound for filming outdoors.

00:28:55.360 --> 00:28:58.320
 It would get inside film studios in London,

00:28:58.320 --> 00:29:00.640
 because it was so much of it.

00:29:00.640 --> 00:29:01.920
 And they didn't know how to get rid of it.

00:29:01.920 --> 00:29:05.280
 So some films in the 1920s that were shot in London

00:29:05.280 --> 00:29:08.080
 had to shoot at night, because you know,

00:29:08.080 --> 00:29:10.640
 you can penetrate darkness with a light.

00:29:10.640 --> 00:29:11.600
 But you can't penetrate it.

00:29:11.600 --> 00:29:14.080
 As anyone who's ever tried to tell on Fog Light's nose,

00:29:14.080 --> 00:29:15.360
 when they do fuck all.

00:29:15.360 --> 00:29:19.120
 Anyone knows that you can't penetrate Fog with any light.

00:29:19.120 --> 00:29:21.920
 So if you wanted to film something, then you had to film it at night.

00:29:21.920 --> 00:29:24.480
 So film schedules would be from 9 p.m. until 6 a.m.

00:29:24.480 --> 00:29:25.680
 Oh my god, it was mad.

00:29:25.680 --> 00:29:28.000
 Alfred Hitchcock's first ever full length film

00:29:28.000 --> 00:29:30.720
 was called The Lodger, a story of the London Fog.

00:29:30.720 --> 00:29:34.400
 It was a bit, it was a big bit of brand Britain.

00:29:34.400 --> 00:29:35.440
 Certainly London, actually.

00:29:35.440 --> 00:29:37.520
 And, you know, any other big industrial cities,

00:29:37.520 --> 00:29:39.360
 because we've, I think we might have mentioned before,

00:29:39.360 --> 00:29:42.640
 the London particular was a term for the Fog.

