 You know where you just couldn't see anything in Manchester.

00:29:47.280 --> 00:29:49.200
 Oh, Andy Burnham, stop trying to make it happen.

00:29:49.200 --> 00:29:52.560
 It is incredible reading about it now,

00:29:52.560 --> 00:29:54.480
 like just how thick the air was.

00:29:54.480 --> 00:29:58.880
 So in 1901, not far from here in Piccadilly Circus,

00:29:58.880 --> 00:30:01.120
 they needed to turn the lights on in Piccadilly,

00:30:01.120 --> 00:30:03.600
 even though the sun was shining, and it was daytime.

00:30:03.600 --> 00:30:06.720
 It was so foggy, you couldn't see where you were going,

00:30:06.720 --> 00:30:08.240
 you couldn't see to drive around.

